<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Multicommodity Network Design Problem with Network Topology</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we formally state the multicommodity network design problem considering the network topology.



Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of physical nodes, and let <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{h}\subseteq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{h}\subseteq G</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of GPUs on node <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{h,h^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{h,h^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the available bandwidth between nodes <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,h^{\prime})\in H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,h^{\prime})\in H</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each executor <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of GPUs required by one replica of <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{s,h}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{s,h}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of replicas of executor <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> placed on node <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.
Continuous variables <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> represent the bandwidth used on node pair <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,h^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,h^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> by traffic between executors <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Achieving request throughput <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> with minimal GPUs can then be formulated as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{x,y,f}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></munder><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{x,y,f}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}\sum_{h\in H}c_{s}\,y_{s,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}\sum_{h\in H}c_{s}\,y_{s,h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.E4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}=\pi_{t}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}=\pi_{t}R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall t\in T," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall t\in T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t\in T}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}\frac{x_{t,p}}{w_{s,t,p}}\;\leq\;\sum_{h\in H}y_{s,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t\in T}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}\frac{x_{t,p}}{w_{s,t,p}}\;\leq\;\sum_{h\in H}y_{s,h}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall s\in S," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall s\in S,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}c_{s}\,y_{s,h}\;\leq\;|G_{h}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}c_{s}\,y_{s,h}\;\leq\;|G_{h}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall h\in H," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall h\in H,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{h,h^{\prime}\in H}f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\;=\;\sum_{t\in T}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}:\\
(s,s^{\prime})\in p\end{subarray}}b_{s,s^{\prime}}\,x_{t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{h,h^{\prime}\in H}f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\;=\;\sum_{t\in T}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}:\\
(s,s^{\prime})\in p\end{subarray}}b_{s,s^{\prime}}\,x_{t,p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall(s,s^{\prime})\in E," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall(s,s^{\prime})\in E,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s,s^{\prime}\in S}f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\;\leq\;B_{h,h^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s,s^{\prime}\in S}f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\;\leq\;B_{h,h^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall h,h^{\prime}\in H," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall h,h^{\prime}\in H,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t,p}\geq 0,\;\;y_{s,h}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0},\;\;f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t,p}\geq 0,\;\;y_{s,h}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0},\;\;f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, our workload has been decomposed into request types <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in T</annotation></semantics></math>, where the proportion of request type <math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (they add up to <math id="A1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>), and each request type has a set of valid executor paths <math id="A1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the executor graph.
For a given target throughput <math id="A1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, the flow-conservation constraint <a href="#A1.E4" title="In Appendix A Multicommodity Network Design Problem with Network Topology ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> requires that the aggregate request rate of type <math id="A1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> equals its share <math id="A1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}R</annotation></semantics></math>, with this rate split across valid paths <math id="A1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> via the variables <math id="A1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The executor-capacity constraint <a href="#A1.E5" title="In Appendix A Multicommodity Network Design Problem with Network Topology ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> ensures that, for each executor <math id="A1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, the total work induced by all request types and paths does not exceed the aggregate capacity provided by its replicas across nodes, as captured by <math id="A1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}y_{s,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}y_{s,h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Node-level GPU capacity is encoded by constraint <a href="#A1.E6" title="In Appendix A Multicommodity Network Design Problem with Network Topology ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, which limits the total number of GPUs consumed on node <math id="A1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> by all executors (each replica of <math id="A1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> GPUs) to the available GPUs <math id="A1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|G_{h}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|G_{h}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
At the network level, constraint <a href="#A1.E7" title="In Appendix A Multicommodity Network Design Problem with Network Topology ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> defines, for each logical executor edge <math id="A1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, the total bandwidth demand induced by all request types and paths, and distributes this demand across node pairs via the variables <math id="A1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s,s^{\prime},h,h^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The link-capacity constraint <a href="#A1.E8" title="In Appendix A Multicommodity Network Design Problem with Network Topology ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> then bounds the aggregate bandwidth consumed on each node pair <math id="A1.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,h^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,h^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> by the available capacity <math id="A1.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{h,h^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{h,h^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Multicommodity Network Design Problem without Network Topology</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we formally state our planner’s multicommodity network design problem.
The resulting formulation is an NP-Hard mixed-integer linear program (MILP).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inputs.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The planner takes the following inputs. We illustrate inputs together with the model example used in Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Request Lifecycle. ‣ 3.2 System Overview ‣ 3 Cornserve Overview ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Model graph:</em> Components <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{\mathrm{E0},\mathrm{E1},\mathrm{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>E0</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E1</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{\mathrm{E0},\mathrm{E1},\mathrm{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and directed edges (e.g., <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{E0}\!\rightarrow\!\mathrm{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E0</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{E0}\!\rightarrow\!\mathrm{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{E1}\!\rightarrow\!\mathrm{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E1</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{E1}\!\rightarrow\!\mathrm{L}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Deployment options:</em> <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are colocated implementations such as <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathrm{E0},\mathrm{E1},\mathrm{L},\mathrm{E0L},\mathrm{E1L},\mathrm{E0E1L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>E0</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E1</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E0L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E1L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E0E1L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathrm{E0},\mathrm{E1},\mathrm{L},\mathrm{E0L},\mathrm{E1L},\mathrm{E0E1L}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, each with component set <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Comp}(s)\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Comp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Comp}(s)\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Workload:</em> Request types <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in T</annotation></semantics></math> given by the actual component sets each request requires (e.g., <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{E0,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{E0,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{L\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{E1,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{E1,L\}</annotation></semantics></math>) with mix <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and total rate <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>; per-type rate is <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}=\pi_{t}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}=\pi_{t}R</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Valid paths:</em> For each <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, a set <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of paths on the executor graph that execute the components in <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> exactly once and respect model order.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:2.0pt;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Profiling information:</em> The profiler measures the per-replica throughput of each deployment option in <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with requests from the workload. Then, we convert the measurements into throughput values for each request type <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s,t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s,t,p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Deriving Throughput Per Request Type ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> is dedicated to this conversion.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decision Variables.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> are integer replicas of executor <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,p}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,p}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is the arrival rate (req/s) of type <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> assigned to path <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Capacity Accounting.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each executor <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, work demand is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}/w_{s,t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}/w_{s,t,p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each replica of executor <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> supplies 1 unit of work.
For demand to not exceed supply, we need</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}\,w_{s,t,p}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\forall s\in S." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}\,w_{s,t,p}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\forall s\in S.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Two Variants.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The planner’s problem has two variants with different objectives:
(1) minimize the number of GPUs <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> given a target throughput <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, or
(2) maximize throughput <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> given a GPU budget <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Minimum Cost Under Target Throughput Variant.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{x,r}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{x,r}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}c_{s}\,r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}c_{s}\,r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.E10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}\;=\;\pi_{t}R\quad\forall t\in T," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}\;=\;\pi_{t}R\quad\forall t\in T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}/w_{s,t,p}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\forall s\in S," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}/w_{s,t,p}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\forall s\in S,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t,p}\geq 0,\;\;r_{s}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t,p}\geq 0,\;\;r_{s}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}=\pi_{t}R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}=\pi_{t}R</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Max Throughput Under Budget Variant.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{x,r,R}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></munder><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{x,r,R}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.E13.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}\;=\;\pi_{t}R\quad\forall t\in T," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}\;=\;\pi_{t}R\quad\forall t\in T,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}/w_{s,t,p}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\forall s\in S," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}x_{t,p}/w_{s,t,p}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\forall s\in S,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}c_{s}r_{s}\;\leq\;B," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s\in S}c_{s}r_{s}\;\leq\;B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t,p}\geq 0,\;\;r_{s}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0},\;\;R\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t,p}\geq 0,\;\;r_{s}\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0},\;\;R\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">where budget <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Both problems are mixed-integer linear programs (MILPs) with a few dozen variables in practice. Integer difficulty comes only from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>; the rest is linear.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Deriving Throughput Per Request Type</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Raw <em id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">rates</em> (e.g., requests/s) do not add across request types, but the <em id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">processing time</em> a replica must spend does.
Consider a deployment option <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> that runs two components <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Comp}(s)=\{c_{1},c_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Comp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Comp}(s)=\{c_{1},c_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> in a time-sharing fashion.
Suppose request type <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> uses only <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and request type <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> uses only <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and both arrive at 1 request/s.
Let <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <em id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per-request-type throughput</em> (req/s) of <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> when it executes the role needed by type <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
The total work <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> must perform is not <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s,t_{1}}+w_{s,t_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s,t_{1}}+w_{s,t_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>; instead it is the <em id="A3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sum of per-request times</em>:</p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{1}}}}_{\text{sec/req for }t_{1}}\;+\;\underbrace{\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{2}}}}_{\text{sec/req for }t_{2}}\quad\text{(seconds).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>sec/req for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>sec/req for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(seconds).</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{1}}}}_{\text{sec/req for }t_{1}}\;+\;\underbrace{\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{2}}}}_{\text{sec/req for }t_{2}}\quad\text{(seconds).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A single replica, every second, can supply at most <math id="A3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> second of work, so in order for work supply to meet demand we need</p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{1}}}+\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{2}}}\;\leq\;1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{1}}}+\frac{1}{w_{s,t_{2}}}\;\leq\;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and more generally, with arbitrary per-type rates <math id="A3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\lambda_{t}\cdot\frac{1}{w_{s,t}}\;\leq\;r_{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\lambda_{t}\cdot\frac{1}{w_{s,t}}\;\leq\;r_{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In our planner this appears path-wise as the node-capacity constraint</p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t\in T}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}\frac{x_{t,p}}{w_{s,t,p}}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\text{for every executor }s," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for every executor </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t\in T}\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{t}}\frac{x_{t,p}}{w_{s,t,p}}\;\leq\;r_{s}\quad\text{for every executor }s,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,p}</annotation></semantics></math> is the rate of type <math id="A3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> assigned to path <math id="A3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s,t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s,t,p}</annotation></semantics></math> is the per-type throughput of <math id="A3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,p)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This additivity in the <em id="A3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">time</em> domain is why we first derive per-request-type processing times from profiling and then invert them to obtain <math id="A3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{s,t,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{s,t,p}</annotation></semantics></math>; it preserves linear processing time accounting at nodes and makes colocated roles (which run on the same GPU in a time-sharing fashion) sum naturally.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm">
<div id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.3.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>
Components <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>; Deployment options <math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with component sets <math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Comp}(s)\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Comp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Comp}(s)\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math>;
Request types <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (each <math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math>); valid paths <math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{P}_{t}\}_{t\in T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{P}_{t}\}_{t\in T}</annotation></semantics></math>;
Single profiled mix <math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{t}\}_{t\in T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{t}\}_{t\in T}</annotation></semantics></math> (fractions, <math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\pi_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\pi_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>);
Per-replica throughput at that mix <math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{s}\}_{s\in S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{s}\}_{s\in S}</annotation></semantics></math> (req/s/replica)

</div>
