</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Communication Overhead</h2>

<figure id="A4.F12" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2512.14098v1/eval-comm-overhead.svg" id="A4.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:314/141;" width="314" height="141"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>The latency of transferring intermediate data between two components under various load when they are disaggregated.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cornserve allows disaggregating model components, which requires communication of intermediate data between components,
such as multimodal embeddings between encoders and LLMs, and hidden states between LLMs and generators.
Figure <a href="#A4.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix D Communication Overhead ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> shows the communication overhead of transferring tensors of different fixed shapes between two components across two nodes.
The sender initiates transfers on GPU tensors at various request rates, while the receiver acknowledges the completion of transfer.
We observe that the communication overhead increases with both the size of the intermediate data and the request rate.
With smaller sizes, the CPU overhead of initiating transfers dominates the communication overhead.
As the size increases, the overhead between copying GPU to CPU memory and transferring data over the network becomes dominant.
Based on the results in §<a href="#S7.SS2" title="7.2 Text and Audio Output Models ‣ 7 Evaluation ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a> and §<a href="#S7.SS3" title="7.3 Text-only Output Models ‣ 7 Evaluation ‣ Cornserve: Efficiently Serving Any-to-Any Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.3</span></a>, Cornserve’s distributed runtime introduces minimal latency overheads.</p>
</div>
</section>
